## Deferred: checked, not worth it now (add `ponytail:` notes only if touched)
- **Allocations in the other benchmarks.** `struct_builder` / `record_batch_builder` are per-element `append` loops at ~1 ns/append and are neutral within noise after T1. About 45% of record_batch_builder time is `page_allocator` doing VirtualAlloc for ~30 tiny allocs per iteration: 60k ns/iter with smp_allocator vs 105k. The library-side fix would fold `BufferStorage` into the data allocation (`buffer.zig:186`); do it only if a profile asks. Do not switch those benchmarks' allocator, because that breaks comparability.
- **IPC writer.** It is memcpy-bound (~6.8 GB/s). Reusing the flatbuffer builder (`ipc/fbs_lite/builder.zig:19-28`) and `initCapacity` hints at `stream_writer.zig:261-264` save only a few allocs per batch.
- **Compressed IPC** copies decompressed bytes up to 4× (`stream_reader.zig:1604-1649`). It is medium-risk offset bookkeeping; do it when a compression benchmark exists.
- **`validateLayout`** scans offsets from 0 instead of the slice window (`array_data.zig:502`). Fixing it loosens the validation contract; skip.
- **`concatValidityBuffer` / bool concat** copy bits one at a time via `isValidAt` (`concat_array_refs.zig` ~:790). It is constant-factor only now that T5 fixed the asymptotics.
- **A direct `take` gather kernel** (no per-index ArrayRef) would turn 534 into ~5 ns/row. It is new per-type kernel code, so do it as its own task if compute matters.
- **Builders regrow from 0 after `finish`** hands its buffers off. This is amortized O(n) after T1.
- **Duplicate `ensureValidityForNull` / `setValidBit` copies** in boolean/view/dictionary/fixed_size. Cleanup only.
- **`FileReader` zero-copy over `self.bytes`.** Same idea as T6; do it when the file path shows up in a profile.

